grund — ground your agents in the spec: §<ID>.<section> citations checked across docs and code.
Usage:  grund <ID>[.<section>]  ·  grund <COMMAND> [ARGS]  ·  grund <COMMAND> -h  ·  grund -V

Query the catalog:
  show          Print a coordinate's lead for agent context (default).  grund FS-login.3
  list          Every declared ID, or the ones nothing cites.           grund list --unused
  refs          Every citation site of a coordinate, as path:line.      grund refs FS-login
  cover         Every scanned file, with the citations in it.           grund cover --format json

Check and author:
  check         Scan a repo or subtree and report findings.             grund check .
  fmt           Normalize citations; maintain links and section locks.  grund fmt --check
  id            Next conflict-free ID for a new declaration.            grund id FS "user login"
  fetch         Materialize one configured external snapshot.           grund fetch TICKET-1234

Set up:
  guide         How to set up and use grund; lists its sections.        grund guide
  init          Scaffold agent instructions + grund.toml.               grund init --scaffold
  config        Validate or show grund.toml; explain a key or a code.   grund config show
  schema        Kinds, places, shapes and citation rules at a glance.   grund schema
  integrations  Print/install clickable-citation integrations.          grund integrations wezterm
  completions   Print shell completion scripts.                         grund completions bash

Guides and examples:  https://github.com/agent-grounds/grund/tree/main/docs/user-facing
